title: Microsoft Intune: Apple ADE Tokens
agents: special
catalog: cloud/microsoft
license: GPLv2
distribution: Christopher Pommer
description:
 This check monitors the expiration status of Apple ADE (Automated Device Enrollment)
 tokens configured in Microsoft Intune.

 The check processes data collected by the {Microsoft Intune} special agent, which
 queries the Microsoft Graph API to retrieve information about all configured ADE
 tokens in the Intune tenant.

 ADE tokens have expiration dates and must be renewed periodically to maintain
 automated device enrollment functionality. The service monitors remaining time
 until expiration and uses configurable thresholds to alert administrators before
 tokens expire.

 Service states are determined by remaining validity time with configurable thresholds.
 Default mapping:

 {OK}: Token expires in more than 14 days

 {WARN}: Token expires within 14 days (default warning threshold)

 {CRIT}: Token expires within 5 days (default critical threshold)

 For expired tokens, the service continues to report critical state and displays
 the expiration timespan as "X ago" format.

 The service details include complete token information such as expiration time,
 token name, unique token ID, token type, and associated Apple ID for administrative
 reference.

 You must configure the {Microsoft Intune} special agent to collect Apple ADE
 token data from your Intune tenant.

item:
 The name of the Apple ADE token as configured in Intune. If multiple tokens
 share the same name, the last 4 characters of the token ID are appended
 for unique identification (e.g., "Apple Business Manager a1b2").

discovery:
 One service is created automatically for each Apple ADE token found in the
 Intune tenant. Services are named "Intune Apple ADE token {token_name}" where
 {token_name} is the configured token name, potentially with ID suffix for uniqueness.